WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.472
earl sold me to a man who owned something called a livery stable.

2
00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:23.217
My new home was far away, which meant I had to travel there by train.

3
00:00:24.438 --> 00:00:25.579
That was a frightening day.

4
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.124
I was used to seeing trains, of course, and never got scared when one rushed past.

5
00:00:33.028 --> 00:00:37.390
But climbing onto one and feeling it roar and tremble all around me was a different matter.

6
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.131
For the first few minutes, I trembled as much as the train did.

7
00:00:42.212 --> 00:00:44.973
After a while, though, I realized there was nothing to fear.

8
00:00:46.273 --> 00:00:47.954
I rode the rest of the way quietly.

9
00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:51.555
But I was very glad to get off!

10
00:00:54.457 --> 00:00:57.518
At the end of my journey, I was taken to the livery stable.

11
00:00:58.778 --> 00:01:02.560
It wasn't as airy and pleasant as my previous homes, but it wasn't too bad.

12
00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:06.118
The owner and his grooms were kind and experienced.

13
00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.422
My new master took a close look at my scarred knees but didn't seem to mind what he

14
00:01:11.482 --> 00:01:15.785
saw. I soon found out what being a livery horse meant.

15
00:01:17.687 --> 00:01:21.550
The master owned lots of horses and many carriages and carts of all different types.

16
00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.952
He hired them out to people who didn't have their own.

17
00:01:26.013 --> 00:01:29.876
The first few times I was hired, my master or one of his men drove me.

18
00:01:32.588 --> 00:01:33.549
That wasn't too bad.

19
00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:36.671
In fact, it wasn't much different from what I was used to.

20
00:01:38.112 --> 00:01:42.715
Once the master saw how steady and reliable I was, he started hiring me out to people who

21
00:01:42.775 --> 00:01:44.116
preferred to drive themselves.

22
00:01:45.277 --> 00:01:46.818
Now that was something different!

23
00:01:48.319 --> 00:01:51.081
Until then I'd only been driven by good drivers.

24
00:01:52.302 --> 00:01:55.665
Even when James was learning, he'd always had John there to help him.

25
00:01:57.046 --> 00:01:59.768
Many of the people who hired me now were not good drivers.

26
00:02:01.584 --> 00:02:04.586
Some liked to keep a very tight hold on the reins at all times.

27
00:02:05.726 --> 00:02:09.108
They never relaxed their pull or allowed me a chance to relax.

28
00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:12.050
Other drivers were just the opposite.

29
00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.492
They let the reins lie loose on my back, hardly touching them at all.

30
00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:20.934
That meant they had no control if I should suddenly rear or stumble.

31
00:02:22.035 --> 00:02:25.977
I wasn't the type of horse to do that, so I had little objection to this type of

32
00:02:26.037 --> 00:02:33.085
driver. Still I sometimes missed the steadying hand of my driver, especially while going downhill.

33
00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:39.109
Besides, the loose-rein drivers were often careless about everything.

34
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.493
I once went a good distance with a stone in my foot before a passing farmer noticed and

35
00:02:44.533 --> 00:02:45.354
stopped to help me.

36
00:02:47.075 --> 00:02:49.616
My own driver never even realized anything was wrong!

37
00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.740
Then there were the customers who cared about nothing but speed.

38
00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.683
They seemed to think we horses were just like trains that could go as far and as fast

39
00:02:59.723 --> 00:03:00.404
as they pleased.

40
00:03:01.568 --> 00:03:04.089
This type of driving wore me out quicker than any other.

41
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.471
So my work at the livery stable differed from day to day.

42
00:03:10.472 --> 00:03:13.253
Sometimes it was pleasant, and other times it was not.

43
00:03:14.853 --> 00:03:18.255
I got to know the other horses there, especially a mare named Peggy.

44
00:03:20.215 --> 00:03:23.237
Peggy was often paired with me when someone wanted to hire a team.

45
00:03:24.457 --> 00:03:26.378
She was a pretty horse with a sweet temper.

46
00:03:27.738 --> 00:03:31.260
The first time we went out together, I noticed she had an odd walk.

47
00:03:32.648 --> 00:03:35.690
It was neither trot nor canter, but a combination of the two.

48
00:03:36.851 --> 00:03:39.293
Every few strides she would add a little jump forward.

49
00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.296
It was very confusing since I had to match my stride to hers.

50
00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:47.719
I finally asked her what made her go in such an odd way.

51
00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:52.202
"I know my gaits are bad," she said, seeming troubled.

52
00:03:52.222 --> 00:03:54.884
"But it's not really my fault.

53
00:03:55.625 --> 00:03:57.006
It's because my legs are short.

54
00:03:57.026 --> 00:04:03.227
That means my stride is short, and I have trouble keeping up with longer-legged horses like you!"

55
00:04:04.928 --> 00:04:08.992
Luckily for Peggy, two women liked her so much that they decided to buy her.

56
00:04:10.353 --> 00:04:12.735
After that I saw Peggy several times out in the street.

57
00:04:13.856 --> 00:04:17.640
She was always pulling her mistresses at a good, steady pace and looking very happy.

58
00:04:19.581 --> 00:04:23.485
I shouldn't make it sound as if I had nothing but poor drivers at the livery stable.

59
00:04:25.006 --> 00:04:26.768
Sometimes I was hired by good horsemen.

60
00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:31.523
One such gentleman liked me so much that he wanted to see what I would be like to

61
00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:32.304
ride as well.

62
00:04:34.285 --> 00:04:38.448
After riding me several times, he asked my master if he would be willing to sell me.

63
00:04:38.468 --> 00:04:43.592
"My friend is looking for a good, safe horse," the man said.

64
00:04:43.612 --> 00:04:46.535
"I think this fellow would be perfect."

65
00:04:47.916 --> 00:04:50.878
"This horse is one of the most reliable in my stable."

66
00:04:51.719 --> 00:04:53.100
My master stroked his chin.

67
00:04:54.592 --> 00:04:58.057
"But I suppose I'd be willing to part with him for the right price."

68
00:04:59.278 --> 00:05:01.141
A deal was struck, and it was settled.

69
00:05:02.182 --> 00:05:03.124
I'd been sold again.
